        "batch50/published_audit.R: ALL 29 PRINTED VALUES OF ALL THREE PUBLISHED FIXTURES REPRODUCED, AND FOR FIG.1 AND FIG.2 AS EXACT FRACTIONS WITH NO TOLERANCE AT ALL. THE EDGE LISTS ARE THE WEAK STEP AND ARE CORROBORATED INDEPENDENTLY BEFORE ANY SCORE IS COMPARED: the 26 ARPA lines read off Fig.6 imply degrees that match Table3's own DC column at ALL 21 nodes, a fatal precondition of the audit, and the Fig.2 reading is pinned by the four printed edge importances. Fixture1, Fig.1 p210: I_e45 = 9/1 at p=0 and 8/3 at p=1, both EXACT FRACTION MATCHES against the printed fractions; this is the lambda regression, since 2p+1 would return 4/3 (NOTE: the candidate_review49 audit said a misreading gives '9/3=3'; recomputed here, U=4 does not depend on lambda, so the wrong reading gives 4/1.5->4/3=1.333333, and the fixture catches it either way). Fixture2, Fig.2 p211: I_e12=8, I_e227=0, I_e45=2, I_e56=4 all match, and L_v2=26/9 and L_v5=52/15 are EXACT FRACTION MATCHES, with L_v5>L_v2 as the paper states. Fixture3, Table3 p217: all 21 printed DIL values reproduce, and THE PAPER'S ROUNDING IS NAMED RATHER THAN ABSORBED INTO A TOLERANCE - both sides are exact multiples of 1e-4 and each value must match under one of exactly two stated printing rules, round-half-away-from-zero at 4dp or truncation at 4dp. ALL 21 MATCH UNDER ROUNDING, 0 need truncation, 0 match neither; largest |computed-printed| is 3.3333333e-05, entirely the paper's own 4dp printing of 23/3 as 7.6667, 41/12 as 3.4167, 89/15 as 5.9333 and 19/6 as 3.1667. The exact rationals behind the column are 61/4, 287/20, 231/20, 23/3, 23/3, 7, 89/15, 7/2, 7/2, 41/12, 41/12, 13/4, 19/6 x5, 3 x3 and 2, each agreeing with the kernel to <1e-12, and TABLE3'S PRINTED ROW ORDER IS ALSO REPRODUCED as the descending order of the computed values. The ARPA graph contains the triangle (1,2,15), found by exhaustive triple enumeration, so the fixture exercises the p>=1 branch. On the same graph the public wrapper agrees with the kernel to 0 and the NetworkX definitional route to 8.8817842e-16. batch50/run_equivalence.R: 126,967 comparisons carrying 760,577 scalar values, ZERO failures; the 99,304 numerical rows carry 732,914 values at a maximum scaled error of 5.703394e-16 against tolerance 1e-11, and the 27,663 invariant rows record a largest STRUCTURAL residual of 2.728484e-12 (the one larger invariant residual, 0.1666667, is lambda_is_not_2p_plus_1, which records the DISTANCE FROM THE WRONG READING on purpose and is reported apart rather than folded into a headline). ALL 5,532 retained fixtures are inside the domain - the measure has no undefined input - and no score is ever NA or non-finite, checked at 5,532. FOUR REFERENCES, THREE OF WHICH SHARE NO DATA STRUCTURE WITH PRODUCTION: (a) 'exact_sets', EXACT fractions.Fraction ARITHMETIC END TO END WITH NO FLOATING POINT ANYWHERE, the graph held as a dict of PYTHON SETS with p from len(nbr[i] & nbr[j]) and eq(3) accumulated by explicit loops - no numpy, no networkx, no matrix of any kind (5,532 comparisons); (b) 'definitional', NetworkX float64, degrees from G.degree, p from networkx.common_neighbors and eqs(2)-(3) accumulated one incident line at a time in a Python loop over G[i], again with no matrix product (5,532); (c) 'matrix_np', dense float64 NumPy reading p off A@A masked by A - this route DOES share production's matrix-product triangle census and its whole-matrix share expression, is NAMED AS SUCH and is not counted as independent (5,532); (d) 'exact_triples', EXACT Fraction again but with p by EXHAUSTIVE ENUMERATION OF EVERY NODE TRIPLE rather than by set algebra or a matrix power, on the n<=20 part of the collection (5,472). All four take the RAW fixture matrix and do their own projection to the simple undirected skeleton, so a projection bug in production cannot hide. THE PARTS ARE CHECKED SEPARATELY, NOT ONLY THE SCORE: the degree column (5,532), the summed line importance (5,532) and the summed contribution (5,532) against set-based references, plus the full per-edge p, I and W matrices entry by entry on n<=20 (5,472 each). INVARIANTS at 5,532 each: U>=0 on every line, verified independently by checking p<=k-1 at both endpoints; every score at least the node's degree; I symmetric while W is not; and THE CONSERVATION IDENTITY sum_i(L_i-k_i)=sum_e I_e, which follows because the two endpoint shares sum to one and which fails if either the share or the K2 branch is wrong (largest residual 2.728484e-12). COMPONENT LOCALITY IS ASSERTED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS on the 5,489 fixtures with n<=30: appending a disjoint triangle-with-pendant leaves every existing score bit-comparable and the appended block scores exactly what it scores alone - DIL is strictly two-hop local, unlike batch48's Lhc. Wrapper, normalized=True, node-permutation, input-projection (weights*13, loops, mode='in', cutoff=1, invert_weights) and an EXPLICIT SYMMETRISATION check each ran at 5,532 comparisons. SEVEN HAND-DERIVED CLOSED FORMS, all independent of every reference route: K_n scores n-1 at every node because p=n-2 makes every U vanish (10 comparisons, n=3..12); a star scores its degree at every node for the same reason, every line touching a leaf (9, m=1..9); a triangle-free k-regular graph scores k+k(k-1)^2/2, so a ring scores 3 and the PETERSEN GRAPH scores 9 (10 + 1); the path P_n scores 1,2.5,3,...,3,2.5,1 (10); and K_{a,b} scores b+b(a-1)(b-1)^2/(a+b-2) on its a-side (5 pairs). THE C_3 BOUNDARY IS ASSERTED RATHER THAN ASSUMED, as in batch48: C_3 is K_3, is not triangle-free, and follows the complete-graph form 2 and not the ring form 3. THE K2 0/0 IS TESTED DIRECTLY as an isolated K2, a K2 beside an isolate and two disjoint K2s: every score is finite, never NA, and the kernel's share matrix is a clean zero, so the 0/0 is never evaluated. Degenerate graphs: empty returns no scores, a singleton and an edgeless graph return zeros, and a disconnected graph needs no rule at all. The Krackhardt kite is retained as a named acceptance fixture in kite_worked.csv, every value computed here. 178 public-test expectations passed with ZERO warnings",
